26	// The tests of the fixture recorder (DEVDESK-511, step 7; Plane DEVDESK-574).
27	// RecordFixtures regenerates the recorded Nexus answers of internal/nexusfixture
28	// from the bench, and it sends the bench credentials to do so: every guard of
29	// the plan has a test here, and every test runs against an httptest server on
30	// the loopback that stands in for the bench. Nothing here reaches a cluster, the
31	// secrets file or the versioned descriptor.
32	//
33	// The contract these tests fix (the plan names the types and the function; the
34	// rest is the simplest reading of its "Step 7" and of the task of DEVDESK-574):
35	//
36	//   - the request to replay is read from the fixture file itself, including a
37	//     request-only file ("# record: pending"); the file is first scanned with
38	//     nexusfixture.CheckLeaks, so a request header outside Host, Authorization
39	//     and Accept, or a query other than n and last, refuses it;
40	//   - everything is validated before the first request: the origins (each must
41	//     be a loopback URL, a key must be a host:port of the descriptor, a fixture
42	//     host must have an origin), the method (GET), the target (closed list of
43	//     path shapes, no query but n and last, no "..", never /manifests/ or
44	//     /blobs/), the credentials of each identity;
45	//   - then the data set is compared with the descriptor, anonymously, on the
46	//     origin of the descriptor's REST host:port (RecordOptions.Descriptor.Hosts[0]
47	//     and REST.NodePort), through ListImagesAnonymously: a listing that differs
48	//     or cannot be read refuses the run (unknown is a refusal, as nothing says
49	//     the bench still holds the data set), before any fixture request;
50	//   - then every fixture is requested once (the exchange method of the client,
51	//     the only sender of credentials), the answer is searched for the real
52	//     passwords (raw, any header or body), redacted, written to text, parsed
53	//     again and checked with CheckLeaks (exact terms: both passwords and both
54	//     Basic encodings, plus DenyTerms), and only when every fixture passed are
55	//     the files written, atomically;
56	//   - every error is a *BenchError (Cause, Check, Err kept for errors.As) that
57	//     names the fixture and, for a leak, the rule, and never a secret;
58	//   - report entries are "<campaign>/<fixture name>", Skipped ones are followed
59	//     by ": <reason>".
60	//
61	// Ambiguities settled here, to be confirmed at review: the dataset check lives
62	// in the library (the plan puts it in the command, step 8); the listing is
63	// anonymous, so a bench that disabled anonymous access cannot be recorded; Dir
64	// empty means nexusfixture.SourceDir(); the HTTP client is not injectable
65	// (guard 1 of guard_test.go forces newClient, and the httptest origin is the
66	// injection point).
